          "page_text": "Abbott has been a part of India's healthcare landscape since 1910, making it one of the oldest and most established health companies in the country. With more than 12,000 employees working across urban centers and rural communities alike, Abbott India serves a vast and varied population — offering over 400 trusted pharmaceutical brands alongside nutritional products, medical devices and diagnostic solutions. The company's headquarters in Mumbai anchors a network that reaches into practically every corner of the subcontinent, reflecting a belief that world-class healthcare should not be a privilege reserved for the few. Abbott India Limited, a publicly listed subsidiary of Abbott Laboratories, is one of India's fastest-growing pharmaceutical companies and a recognized leader in women's health, gastroenterology, metabolic conditions, neurology and vaccines. The company has invested in local manufacturing for its two largest businesses — nutrition and pharmaceuticals — because building for India means building in India. That commitment to local production ensures that products are designed and made with the specific needs of Indian consumers in mind, from the nutritional requirements of infants and young children to the health challenges facing aging adults. For more than 115 years, Abbott in India has strived to be closer to the people it serves. That closeness shapes everything — the products developed, the communities supported and the partnerships forged with healthcare professionals across the country. From creating excellent workplaces recognized by leading industry bodies to addressing the health needs of both rural and urban populations, Abbott in India takes pride in the lasting difference it makes every day. Products and Solutions * [Overview][1] * [Diabetes][2] * [Nutrition][3] * [Diagnostics Testing][4] * [Cardiovascular][5] * [Pain and Movement][6] * [Biowearables][7] * [Medicines][8] * [All Products][9] Need Help? * [Where to Buy][