rchived releases, quarterly results, annual reports and financial statements. Initiatives Investor Centre. [What’s latest with Dabur][71] * [Share Information][72] * [Dabur Share Price][73] * [Share Graph][74] * [Share Series][75] * [Investment Calculator][76] * [Financial Information][77] * [Digital Annual Report][78] * [Reports][79] * [Results][80] * [10 Year Highlights][81] * [Corporate Governance][82] * [Details Of Business][83] * [Corporate Governance Reports][84] * [Policies and Related Documents][85] * [Board of Directors][86] * [Committees of Board of Directors][87] * [Independent Directors][88] * [Investor Information][89] * [Shareholding Pattern][90] * [Scheme of Arrangement ][91] * [Schedule of Analyst/Investor Meet, Presentations & Recordings][92] * [Notices & Voting Results][93] * [Statutory Filings][94] * [Newspaper Publications][95] * [Shareholder Services][96] * [Unclaimed Dividend and Shares][97] * [Esops][98] * [Annual Return][99] * [Non Convertible Debentures][100] * [Commercial Paper][101] * [Disclosures Under Regulation 46 and 62 Sebi Lodr Regulations 2015][102] * Newsroom button [Newsroom] Welcome to Dabur Media Centre. In this section, you’ll find our latest Press Releases arranged in a chronological order. The Press Releases have been further [Latest From Dabur][103] * [Dabur in the News][104] * [Press Releases][105] * [Media Library][106] * Ayurveda & you button [Newsroom] Our curated Collection of Ayurvedic knowledge for you. We at Dabur are working towards helping people lead a healthy and balanced life. [Explore the Blog][107] * [Ayurveda & Science][108] * [What is Ayurveda][109] * [Ayurvedic Body Types][110] * [Ayurvedic & Medicinal Plants][111] * [Ayurvedic Home Remedies][112] * Sustainability button [Newsroom] Dabur has been engaged in community development activities since 1994 and is committed to making a positive contribution to the communities where we source, live, work and sell our products. * [CSR At Dabur][113] * [Life Cycle Assessment][114] * [Water Risk Assessment][115] * [ESG Microsite][116] * Join Us button [test] At Dabur, we are very passionate about winning and this has been engrained in DNA of the organization. [Life At dabur][117] * [How We Hire][118] * [Our Teams][119] * [Dabur Campus Bridge][120] * [Explore Opportunities][121] * Support button [test] Got a question? We'd love to hear from you. . [Write to us][122] * [Contact Information][123] * [Addresses][124] * [Branch Office][125] * [Contact Head - Private Labels][126] * [Factories][127] * [Overseas Office][128] * [Subsidiaries][129] * [Apply for Distribution][130] * [Private Labels][131] * [Revised Price List][132] * [Dabur Shop][133] ## Header Right Menu * [Dabur Arogya][134] search Search Search [Dabur Region] * [GCC][135] * [Turkey & CIS][136] * [U.S.A and Americas][137] * [Pakistan and West Asia][138] * [UK & Europe][139] ## Search Search Search ### At Dabur,we believe that goodness is something that’s worth sharing with the world. ### We like to treat mother nature with the respect a mother deserves. ### Making ancient Ayurveda and modern science work together, is the secret to everything we make. # DABUR - WORLD'S LEADING AYURVEDA COMPANY ## EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR We know it’s not easy to stay healthy in a world like ours. It means eating the right things, taking time off, and putting in the hours. It means living in harmony with your mind, body, and soul. Our hope is to make this path to wellness easier with a little help from our [Ayurvedic products][140]. There’s a lot that goes into a Dabur product. It begins with extensive research that can take months or even years. We then gather the best ingredients by tapping the vast goodness of nature. There’s a lot of trial and a whole lot of effort until we finally find a formula that truly works for you. This is what keeps us going every day. 250 + AYURVEDIC PRODUCTS 140 YEARS OF LEGACY AND QUALITY EXPERIENCE 6.9 MILLION RETAIL OUTLETS 120 COUNTRIES WITH DABUR PRODUCTS * [Know Our Story][141] ##### WHAT WE DO ### Ancient Ayurveda met modern science. And together they went and built a legacy. Gathering the choicest, natural ingredients is important. But you also need to know how to blend them to create a quality health product. That’s why we rely on the traditional knowledge of Ayurveda and the expertise of modern-day science. And quite honestly, it’s the very foundation of everything we’ve built ever since. * [Explore Ayurveda][142] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR Your touch + Dabur Lal Tail = One healthy baby [Explore Brand][143] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR The dream team of honey and herbs to make sure sore throats don't slow you down. [Explore Brand][144] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR For hair that radiates 'fabulous' every day, you need a shampoo that can do it all with the goodness of nature. [Explore Brand][145] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR If your stomach is upset, we know how to make it come around. [Explore Brand][146] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR Having good teeth is sort of a great tradition for us. [Explore Brand][147] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR For hair that's as strong as you are. Seriously. [Explore Brand][148] [amla hair oil] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR Real fruit juice. But without all the peeling, and squeezing and stuff. [Explore Brand][149] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR Think a whole lot of immunity. Now double that. [Explore Brand][150] EXPLORE THE WORLD OF DABUR Sweet taste, natural glow. There's a reason why we call all that we love, honey. [Explore Brand][151] * [Previous][152] * [Next][153] ## OUR INGREDIENTS ### What’s on the inside is what matters the most. Of course, the quality of ingredients has a huge impact on how our products work. But we go beyond “the best” and “the rare”. We like our ingredients to be as natural and fresh as possible, just like the conversations we like to have. [ #### Chitrak A profusely branched perennial shrub with alternate leaves. The plant is available throughout India wildly and is also cultivated in gardens for its brilliant inflorescence. Root and root bark of the plant are used in preparation of various Ayurvedic medi ][154] [ #### Varun plant A moderate sized deciduous tree found wild but also cultivated throughout India. Bark of the tree is used in Ayurveda. ][155] [ #### tamalpatra A moderate sized tree with aromatic leaves and bark found growing wild in tropical and subtropical Himalayas and north-eastern Himalayas. ][156] [ #### shalai guggal A middle-sized tree with alternate deciduous sessile leaves. It is found in the forests of western and central India. Gum resin from the stem is used medicinally. ][157] [ #### PIPPALI PLANT A slender aromatic climber having flowers in solitary spikes forming small red berries sunken in solid fleshy spike. The spike is tremendously used in Ayurveda for the preparation of number of formulations. ][158] [ #### MULETHI A hardy leguminous undershrub attaining the height of about 3 meter with compressed pods. It is found growing wild in many Asian countries and is also cultivated at small scales in India, Iran, Afghanistan etc. The root tastes sweet and is used in Ayurvedic. ][159] [ #### KULANJAN PLANT Greater galangal grows to a height of 1.8 m and has long, elegant, blade-like leaves. The flowers are green and white with red tips. Rhizome is built up from cylindrical subunits (circular cross-section), whose pale-reddish surface is characteristicall ][160] [ #### JIMIKAND PLANT A tuberous, stout, indigenous herb, 1.0-1.5 m found almost throughout India. Tubers depressed, globose or hemispherical, dark brown out side, pale dull brown, sometimes almost white, with numerous long roots; leaves solitary, tripartite, 30-90 cm broad ][161] [ #### DALCHINI PLANT A small evergreen tree with aromatic bark of about 6-8 m in height found growing wild in southern coastal regions of India. The bark is used as culinary spice and also in medicines. ][162] [ #### BHOJPATRA PLANT A moderate sized tree with papery brownish-white bark found in groups at timberline in Himalayas. The thin layers of bark are used in Ayurveda. ][163] [ #### ATEES A perennial erect herb with greenish-blue flower found wild in alpine and sub-alpine Himalayas. Root of the herb is used in Ayurveda. ][164] [ #### AMLA A middle sized deciduous tree with green globose fruits found wild throughout tropical India. The tree is extensively cultivated these days in many parts of India for its fruits. ][165] Previous Next [Know More][166] ### The only way to care for your body, is to know how to understand it. According to the [science of Ayurveda][167], our world is made up of five elements - ether, water, air, earth, and fire. Each of us contains a unique blend of these elements, or doshas - [vata][168], [pitta][169] and [kapha][170]. The key to health and wellness lies in balancing the three. bottom Find Your Vata - Pitta - Kapha index here Last test was taken 5 minutes ago. [Take The Test Now][171] # DABUR AROGYA ## Need to talk to a Doctor? When it comes to health, we know that investing in a quality product is just one step among many. That’s why we created Dabur Arogya, an initiative which helps you consult with doctors who are equipped to guide you through your wellness journey, with ease. Know more about Ayurveda with our curated collection of Ayurvedic knowledge * [Discover More][172] 2,11,327 + CONSUMERS HELPED BY OUR DOCTORS 26,031 DOCTORS ASSOCIATED WITH US 317 + ARTICLES, LIVE WORKSHOPS AND SESSIONS Know your symptoms and consult a doctor online for your personalis",
